# Sisyphus environment — copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored.

#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Loaded at daemon/CLI startup (core/env.py). Precedence: a variable already set
# in the shell/launchd wins over .env.

# Tokens, keys and service addresses do NOT go here. Enter them in the UI —
# Integrations → Keys & tokens — which keeps them in Sisyphus's own keychain,
# out of reach of every agent. A credential put in this file is ignored (the
# page lists it and offers to move it).

# Optional: override where the daemon keeps its data (db, repos, backups).
# Defaults to <repo>/workspace.
# WORKSPACE_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/workspace
